(7327761, 1144012, 163430, '<td valign="top">I like the ligthing and the composition, but the processing doesn''t float my boat.</td>', 'I like the ligthing and the composition, but the processing doesn''t float my boat.', '2015-03-17 17:39:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(7327762, 1143974, 163430, '<td valign="top">That reflection is really killing this excellent idea for me.</td>', 'That reflection is really killing this excellent idea for me.', '2015-03-17 17:43:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(7327763, 1143570, 163430, '<td valign="top">Good one. Hats down to the idea and the execution.<br/>I almost tried a similar approach. A shot through the vertical viewfinder of a TLR. Instead of a cityscape, the subject''s subject would have been another vintage camera. The orientation and the size of the viewfinder made it a very tough shot and i gave up. I wouldn''t have been as effective as yours, anyway.</td>', 'Good one. Hats down to the idea and the execution.I almost tried a similar approach. A shot through the vertical viewfinder of a TLR. Instead of a cityscape, the subject''s subject would have been another vintage camera. The orientation and the size of the viewfinder made it a very tough shot and i gave up. I wouldn''t have been as effective as yours, anyway.', '2015-03-17 17:43:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(7327764, 1144001, 163430, '<td valign="top">One of the rare entries that emphasized the "portrait" part of the challenge. I like that. Maybe the golden eyelashes were a bit of an overkill, but maybe not :-)</td>', 'One of the rare entries that emphasized the "portrait" part of the challenge. I like that. Maybe the golden eyelashes were a bit of an overkill, but maybe not :-)', '2015-03-17 17:44:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(7327766, 1143596, 163430, '<td valign="top">I love the tight crop and the DoF. <br/> <br/>The lighting in general is good, except for the mixed colours. The combination of bluish, white and yellowish highlights is a bit distracting. If it wasn''t correctable in post, you should have gone with B&amp;W (maybe recover the color on the red elements afterwards). Unless, of course, the mixed lighting was your intention. A bit more microcontrast/structure/clarity would have been nice, as well.<br/> <br/>All in all, a solid take on the camera portrait challenge.</td>', 'I love the tight crop and the DoF.  The lighting in general is good, except for the mixed colours. The combination of bluish, white and yellowish highlights is a bit distracting. If it wasn''t correctable in post, you should have gone with B&W (maybe recover the color on the red elements afterwards). Unless, of course, the mixed lighting was your intention. A bit more microcontrast/structure/clarity would have been nice, as well. All in all, a solid take on the camera portrait challenge.', '2015-03-17 17:53:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(7327768, 1144003, 163430, '<td valign="top">Excellent lighting. I love the red strap and the way the the foreground gradually blends into the background. The subject is beautiful, as well.<br/> <br/>A bit more depth would benefit the image and maybe cropping out a bit from the bottom.<br/> <br/>As for that hint of a reflection at the bottom, i would prefer if it was either not there or more prominent, but it''s not a distracting element in the image as it is.</td>', 'Excellent lighting. I love the red strap and the way the the foreground gradually blends into the background. The subject is beautiful, as well. A bit more depth would benefit the image and maybe cropping out a bit from the bottom. As for that hint of a reflection at the bottom, i would prefer if it was either not there or more prominent, but it''s not a distracting element in the image as it is.', '2015-03-17 18:02:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(7327778, 1143946, 163430, '<td valign="top">I can''t help but notice that twin lens reflex cameras are beautiful portrait subjects. There are a bunch of TLR entries in this challenge (mine included).<br/> <br/>Lighting is spot on, as well as the sharpness and DoF. Colours work nice here, as well.</td>', 'I can''t help but notice that twin lens reflex cameras are beautiful portrait subjects. There are a bunch of TLR entries in this challenge (mine included). Lighting is spot on, as well as the sharpness and DoF. Colours work nice here, as well.', '2015-03-17 18:10:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(7327781, 1143947, 163430, '<td valign="top">27 exposures? I have never seen a film with 27 exposures. What kind of film it uses, 110? It might as well be 135 (35mm) judging by the size of the camera.</td>', '27 exposures? I have never seen a film with 27 exposures. What kind of film it uses, 110? It might as well be 135 (35mm) judging by the size of the camera.', '2015-03-17 18:12:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(7327785, 1143555, 163430, '<td valign="top">Nice inclusion of a human element. The lighting is good, as well as the DoF.</td>', 'Nice inclusion of a human element. The lighting is good, as well as the DoF.', '2015-03-17 18:14:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(7327799, 1143870, 163430, '<td valign="top">One of the rare specimens of a modern digital camera in the challenge. The majority of us opted for a vintage subject.<br/> <br/>The B&amp;W approach works well, but the inclusion of colour might have been effective as well. Nikon DSLR cameras have that red triangular element on the grip, below the shutter button, that might be interesting element, as well as the gold on the topp of the lens. DoF is spot-on. <br/> <br/>There is some visible noise on the lens cap and the very front of the lens that is a bit distracting.</td>', 'One of the rare specimens of a modern digital camera in the challenge. The majority of us opted for a vintage subject. The B&W approach works well, but the inclusion of colour might have been effective as well. Nikon DSLR cameras have that red triangular element on the grip, below the shutter button, that might be interesting element, as well as the gold on the topp of the lens. DoF is spot-on.  There is some visible noise on the lens cap and the very front of the lens that is a bit distracting.', '2015-03-17 18:22:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(7327811, 1144004, 163430, '<td valign="top">The mixed-colour lighting is a white balance nightmare. Unless this is a desired effect, B&amp;W might be a solution for this.<br/> <br/>Nice tight crop, BTW. Brave on your side not including the lens. It is a bit like a human portrait without including the eyes. It might work.</td>', 'The mixed-colour lighting is a white balance nightmare. Unless this is a desired effect, B&W might be a solution for this. Nice tight crop, BTW. Brave on your side not including the lens. It is a bit like a human portrait without including the eyes. It might work.', '2015-03-17 18:27:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(7327816, 1143943, 163430, '<td valign="top">Interesting concept. Candid portrait of a camera :-)<br/> <br/>The cables are distracting and the image lacks sharpness.</td>', 'Interesting concept. Candid portrait of a camera :-) The cables are distracting and the image lacks sharpness.', '2015-03-17 18:30:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(7327827, 1143988, 163430, '<td valign="top">Nicely seen with matching lighting and processing.</td>', 'Nicely seen with matching lighting and processing.', '2015-03-17 18:36:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(7327839, 1143755, 163430, '<td valign="top">Interesting choice of subject. Not being a camera per se is not why this image doesn''t work for me. I actually think that it''s quite an original idea and meets the challenge well. It''s the combination of the exposure, the distorted base of the lamp and the processing.<br/> <br/>Sorry :-(</td>', 'Interesting choice of subject. Not being a camera per se is not why this image doesn''t work for me. I actually think that it''s quite an original idea and meets the challenge well. It''s the combination of the exposure, the distorted base of the lamp and the processing. Sorry :-(', '2015-03-17 18:44:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(7327849, 1143961, 163430, '<td valign="top">Nice subject(s) and processing resembles of a Polaroid shot.<br/> <br/>Having said that, i would have:<br/>- Cropped the distracting negative space from above. This would have the added bonus of making the image more-or-less Polaroid aspect ratio.<br/>- Added a Polaroid style white border<br/>- (maybe) Asked the model to tuck in her right (camera left) leg so it doesn''t get chopped off.</td>', 'Nice subject(s) and processing resembles of a Polaroid shot. Having said that, i would have:- Cropped the distracting negative space from above. This would have the added bonus of making the image more-or-less Polaroid aspect ratio.- Added a Polaroid style white border- (maybe) Asked the model to tuck in her right (camera left) leg so it doesn''t get chopped off.', '2015-03-17 18:50:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(7327852, 1143960, 163430, '<td valign="top">I wanted to do an image like this with an TLR as a subject. I gave up after realizing that i cannot do anything even close to Gregory Heisler''s self portrait done at GPP 2012 (<a href="//gulfphotoplus.com/limited/image/4/GPP-Self-Portrait-2012" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//gulfphotoplus.com/limited/image/4/GPP-Self-Portrait-2012</a>).</td>', 'I wanted to do an image like this with an TLR as a subject. I gave up after realizing that i cannot do anything even close to Gregory Heisler''s self portrait done at GPP 2012 (//gulfphotoplus.com/limited/image/4/GPP-Self-Portrait-2012).', '2015-03-17 18:58:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(7327853, 1143966, 163430, '<td valign="top">Interesting subject, but a bit soft.</td>', 'Interesting subject, but a bit soft.', '2015-03-17 19:05:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(7327854, 1143730, 163430, '<td valign="top">Too much processing for my taste. It looks more like an illustration or a drawing than a photo. The blown out highlights on the D50 badge is distracting, as well.</td>', 'Too much processing for my taste. It looks more like an illustration or a drawing than a photo. The blown out highlights on the D50 badge is distracting, as well.', '2015-03-17 19:08:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(7327855, 1144002, 163430, '<td valign="top">The lass is holding the camera the wrong way :-)<br/> <br/>It''s a nice candid portrait that would have been a better entry for the <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/challenge_submit.php?CHALLENGE_ID=2076" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Street Photography in Black and White II</a> than this challenge.</td>', 'The lass is holding the camera the wrong way :-) It''s a nice candid portrait that would have been a better entry for the Street Photography in Black and White II than this challenge.', '2015-03-17 19:12:42.000000', NULL, 1),
