(7331962, 1143995, 103032, '<td valign="top">Nicely done Wendy.  When the Challenge came up, I was thinking something similar (but life got in the way).  My dad has a Yashica 635.  I remember him shooting B&amp;W with that Yashica all the time.  Must be that generation with their TLRs...<br/> <br/>Really enjoy reading the notes you put with your photos.</td>', 'Nicely done Wendy.  When the Challenge came up, I was thinking something similar (but life got in the way).  My dad has a Yashica 635.  I remember him shooting B&W with that Yashica all the time.  Must be that generation with their TLRs... Really enjoy reading the notes you put with your photos.', '2015-03-21 20:28:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(7334998, 1143943, 30861, '<td valign="top">Geeze, Jeb, ain''t you the picture of a middle-aged rebel :-)</td>', 'Geeze, Jeb, ain''t you the picture of a middle-aged rebel :-)', '2015-03-27 18:39:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(7394632, 1143555, 25024, '<td valign="top">*Hello from Sid and the Critique Club*<br/> <br/>A pleasing portrait that meets the challenge well.<br/> <br/>Thank you for your quirky and helpful notes, you have correctly identified the technical aspects of your shot that would benefit from altered settings, ie., aperture priority and lower ISO etc., Having said that the end result is not significantly affected and is still a pleasing result that needs little improvement<br/> <br/>Your composition is good with empty space for the camera to look into, the background is neutral without any distractions and the generally high key effect is complimentary to the white hair of your subject. To be honest apart from the altered settings there''s not a lot else to add, well done, Sid</td>', '*Hello from Sid and the Critique Club* A pleasing portrait that meets the challenge well. Thank you for your quirky and helpful notes, you have correctly identified the technical aspects of your shot that would benefit from altered settings, ie., aperture priority and lower ISO etc., Having said that the end result is not significantly affected and is still a pleasing result that needs little improvement Your composition is good with empty space for the camera to look into, the background is neutral without any distractions and the generally high key effect is complimentary to the white hair of your subject. To be honest apart from the altered settings there''s not a lot else to add, well done, Sid', '2015-08-03 06:07:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(7569988, 1144002, 152252, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by damjanev:</b></div><hr/><i> The lass is holding the camera the wrong way :-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You never adjust the focus manually?</td>', 'Originally posted by damjanev: The lass is holding the camera the wrong way :-)   You never adjust the focus manually?', '2018-06-02 11:40:34.000000', NULL, 0);
